# CCTP Bridge Workflow — environment variables
#
# SHARED WITH THE GASLESS WORKFLOW
# -----------------
# This .env is identical in schema to gasless-workflow/.env.
# The simplest setup is to symlink the gasless workflow's file:
#
#   cd cctp-bridge
#   ln -s ../gasless-workflow/.env .env
#
# Or copy it:
#   cp ../gasless-workflow/.env .env
#
# Both OWNER_PRIVATE_KEY and RECIPIENT_PRIVATE_KEY must be present.
# All CCTP contract addresses below are pre-populated with testnet values
# and match the values already in gasless-workflow/.env.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE IS USED FOR
# --------------------------
# 1. scripts/aws-setup.mjs  — reads OWNER_PRIVATE_KEY and RECIPIENT_PRIVATE_KEY
#    to upsert paymaster-key-owner and paymaster-key-recipient in Secrets Manager.
# 2. local-test/env.json       — these same values are injected into `sam local invoke`
#    via --env-vars (the private keys override Secrets Manager during local testing).
#
# NOTE: local-test/env.json already has all contract addresses hard-coded.
# This .env is only needed for aws-setup.mjs and any ad-hoc Node scripts.

# ── Wallet keys ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
OWNER_PRIVATE_KEY=0x<owner private key>
OWNER_ADDRESS=0x<owner EOA address>

RECIPIENT_PRIVATE_KEY=0x<recipient private key>
RECIPIENT_ADDRESS=0x<recipient EOA address>

# ── Ethereum Sepolia (Source chain) ────────────────────────────────────────────
ETH_USDC_ADDRESS=0x1c7D4B196Cb0C7B01d743Fbc6116a902379C7238
ETH_PAYMASTER_ADDRESS=0x3BA9A96eE3eFf3A69E2B18886AcF52027EFF8966
